WEBVTT

00:00:00.046 --> 00:00:01.753
Now imagine the store is unavailable.

00:00:02.136 --> 00:00:04.540
The validation service cannot truthfully report a

00:00:04.598 --> 00:00:05.596
successful save.

00:00:06.037 --> 00:00:08.255
It returns a failure the form can display.

00:00:08.696 --> 00:00:11.424
The visitor sees an explanation and an appropriate next

00:00:11.447 --> 00:00:15.024
step; the owner sees an operator diagnostic that avoids

00:00:15.058 --> 00:00:16.951
exposing the visitor's private details.

00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:20.573
Once storage returns, the visitor can retry under the

00:00:20.631 --> 00:00:22.280
agreed duplicate-handling rule.

00:00:22.884 --> 00:00:25.891
Drawing this path reveals a design need that a diagram of

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.632
only successful arrows would miss.
